1
00:00:09,005 --> 00:00:12,845
C'est bon. Adjani reste à ASK, et moi je cours après Nathalie Baye.
It's okay. Adjani is staying at ASK,
and I'm hunting Nathalie Baye.

2
00:00:12,925 --> 00:00:14,445
Ça se passe comment avec Dubosc ?
How are things with Dubosc?

3
00:00:14,525 --> 00:00:16,405
Mon GPS dit qu'il est à 200m.
My GPS says he's 200m away.

4
00:00:16,485 --> 00:00:19,845
Je suis sur le tournage. Je trouve le Centre Communautaire et c'est bon.
I'm on the set. I have to find
the Community Center and we're good.

5
00:00:19,925 --> 00:00:21,165
Ne foire pas ça cette fois.
Don't mess it up this time.

6
00:00:21,244 --> 00:00:24,685
T'as déjà perdu Mimie Mathy, on peut pas se permettre de perdre Franck Dubosc.
You already lost Mimie Mathy,
we can't afford to lose Franck Dubosc.

7
00:00:24,765 --> 00:00:26,125
On peut rien se permettre !
We can't afford anything!

8
00:00:26,245 --> 00:00:27,285
T'inquiète pas...
Don't worry...

9
00:00:27,365 --> 00:00:29,045
Il voulait tourner dans un film d'auteur,
He wanted to be in an arthouse film,

10
00:00:29,125 --> 00:00:30,645
il va être de super bonne humeur !
he'll to be in a great mood!

11
00:00:30,725 --> 00:00:32,845
J'en peux plus. J'en ai marre.
I can't take it anymore. I've had it.

12
00:00:34,245 --> 00:00:35,085
T'en as marre ?
You've had it?

13
00:00:36,205 --> 00:00:37,164
De quoi ?
With what?

14
00:00:38,045 --> 00:00:39,365
Tu sais ce que ça veut dire ?
Do you know what it means?

15
00:00:40,445 --> 00:00:42,245
Tu t'attendais à m'apprendre la vie ?
Did you expect to teach me about life?

16
00:00:43,045 --> 00:00:44,605
T'y connais quoi à la vie ?
What do you know about life?

17
00:00:45,245 --> 00:00:47,045
Tu sais rien, espèce d'enfoiré.
You don't know anything, piece of shit.

18
00:00:47,925 --> 00:00:49,405
Coupez ! C'était fabuleux.
Cut! That was fabulous.

19
00:00:49,485 --> 00:00:50,485
Génial.
Awesome.

20
00:00:50,565 --> 00:00:52,325
« Enfoiré » n'était pas dans le scénario.
"Piece of shit" wasn't in the script.

21
00:00:52,405 --> 00:00:54,845
C'était brillant. On change de décor
It was brilliant. Let's change the set

22
00:00:54,925 --> 00:00:56,365
pendant que je réécris la prochaine scène !
while I rewrite the next scene!

23
00:00:56,445 --> 00:00:57,485
Dylan, viens avec moi.
Dylan, come with me.

24
00:00:58,365 --> 00:01:00,485
On change le plan...
Let's change the shot...

25
00:01:01,045 --> 00:01:03,405
Bravo. Vraiment. C'était incroyable.
Well done. Really. That was amazing.

26
00:01:03,485 --> 00:01:04,845
Oh... merci. C'est gentil.
Oh... thanks. That's nice.

27
00:01:05,805 --> 00:01:08,245
Je suis Gabriel Sarda. Je suis agent chez ASK.
I'm Gabriel Sarda. I'm an agent with ASK.

28
00:01:09,524 --> 00:01:10,965
L'assistant de Samuel ?
Samuel's assistant?

29
00:01:11,045 --> 00:01:12,525
C'était il y a longtemps.
That was a long time ago.

30
00:01:12,965 --> 00:01:16,205
Ça fait dix ans que je suis agent senior. En fait...
I've been a senior agent
for ten years now. In fact...

31
00:01:16,685 --> 00:01:19,045
Je suis venu parler de ton avenir chez ASK...
I came to talk
about your future with ASK...

32
00:01:19,125 --> 00:01:20,685
ASK ou ailleurs.
ASK or some other place.

33
00:01:20,765 --> 00:01:22,165
J'étais proche de Mathias.
I was close with Mathias.

34
00:01:22,245 --> 00:01:24,205
Mathias et moi c'est pareil.
Mathias and me are the same.

35
00:01:24,285 --> 00:01:25,605
On est comme des frères !
We're like brothers!

36
00:01:25,685 --> 00:01:29,045
C'est moi, en fait, qui ai proposé ce rôle pour toi.
As a matter of fact, I was the one
who suggested this role for you.

37
00:01:29,685 --> 00:01:32,005
Donc c'est toi le responsable de ce bordel ?
So you're responsible for this mess?

38
00:01:32,085 --> 00:01:33,365
Ça se passe mal ?
It's not going well?

39
00:01:33,445 --> 00:01:35,445
Non, mais c'est le pire tournage de ma vie.
It is,
but it's the worst shoot of my life.

40
00:01:35,525 --> 00:01:37,805
... « Bro », comme on dit ici. Fais gaffe.
... "Bro," as they say around here.
Careful.

41
00:01:37,885 --> 00:01:39,645
Je sais pas du tout ce que je fais.
I don't have a clue what I'm doing.

42
00:01:40,085 --> 00:01:43,805
La réalisatrice réécrit les scènes toutes les deux secondes...
The director rewrites scenes
every two seconds...

43
00:01:44,605 --> 00:01:46,805
Parfois on ne dit pas notre texte, on reste silencieux.
Sometimes we don't say our lines,
we stay silent.

44
00:01:46,885 --> 00:01:48,805
Elle a même tourné une scène avec son téléphone.
She even shot a scene with her phone.

45
00:01:48,885 --> 00:01:52,205
Franck, c'est ouf, ça commence à avoir du groove. J'adore !
Franck, it's awesome, it's starting
to have some groove. I'm digging it!

46
00:01:52,285 --> 00:01:54,285
Mais il y a quelque chose qui cloche.
But something's not right.

47
00:01:54,365 --> 00:01:55,365
Tu vois quand...
You know when...

48
00:01:56,165 --> 00:01:57,125
Quand tu...
When you...

49
00:01:58,205 --> 00:02:00,045
-Quand je « joue » ? -Voilà, c'est ça.
-When I "act"?
-Yeah, that's it.

50
00:02:00,125 --> 00:02:02,045
Donc si tu pouvais jouer... moins.
So if you could act... less.

51
00:02:02,925 --> 00:02:04,205
Sinon c'était bien.
Otherwise it was great.

52
00:02:04,685 --> 00:02:07,045
Elle dit que sinon c'est bien. C'est positif.
She said that otherwise it's great.
That's positive.

53
00:02:07,605 --> 00:02:10,445
Franck ! Je comprends que ça puisse déstabiliser, vraiment !
Franck! I get
that it can be unsettling, I do!

54
00:02:10,525 --> 00:02:14,965
Mais ça en vaut la peine. Écoute, tu tournes avec une réalisatrice qui a une vision.
But it's worth it. Listen, you're shooting
with a director who was vision.

55
00:02:15,044 --> 00:02:18,845
Et il y a le gamin, Dylan Charif. Il a eu le César du meilleur espoir.
And there's the kid, Dylan Charif.
He got the César for best emergent actor.

56
00:02:18,925 --> 00:02:20,525
-Ça doit être inspirant. -Oh, oui.
-It must be inspiring.
-Oh, yes.

57
00:02:20,605 --> 00:02:22,045
Très inspirant. Ouais !
Very inspiring. Yeah!

58
00:02:22,125 --> 00:02:24,605
Il est convaincu d'être l'avenir du cinéma français.
He's convinced
he's the future of French cinema.

59
00:02:24,685 --> 00:02:26,125
Et moi je suis quoi pour lui ?
So what am I to him?

60
00:02:27,445 --> 00:02:30,045
Bah. Un vieux has-been qui tourne des films en Speedo.
Well. I'm an old has-been
who shoots films in his Speedos.

61
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:33,005
Il se moque de moi toute la journée, je n'en peux plus.
He ridicules me all day long,
I can't stand it.

62
00:02:33,605 --> 00:02:36,565
Je veux dire... Ça suffit, cette merde.
I mean... Enough of this shit.

63
00:02:36,645 --> 00:02:38,845
C'est... J'en ai assez.
It's... I've had enough.

64
00:02:38,925 --> 00:02:41,365
Pour avoir cru Mathias quand il m'a dit,
To think I believed Mathias when he said,

65
00:02:41,445 --> 00:02:43,445
"Un tournant dans ta carrière." "Ah ouais."
"A turning point in your career."
"Oh, yeah."

66
00:02:43,525 --> 00:02:45,645
Il a raison, hein. Ça vaut le coup.
He's right, he is. It's worth it.

67
00:02:45,725 --> 00:02:47,205
Ce pourrait être ton Tchao Pantin.
This could be your Tchao Pantin.

68
00:02:47,285 --> 00:02:50,605
Si ça continue, ce sera "Ciao, au revoir." Voilà.
Well, if this keeps up, it's going to be
"Ciao, goodbye." There.

69
00:02:51,085 --> 00:02:52,885
Je ne suis pas fait pour le cinéma d'auteur.
I'm not cut out for arthouse films.

70
00:02:52,965 --> 00:02:55,325
Je n'ai rien à faire ici. C'était une erreur.
I don't belong here. This was a mistake.

71
00:02:55,405 --> 00:02:57,445
Hé ! "Personne n'attend Patrick ?"
Hey! "No one waits for Patrick?"

72
00:02:58,365 --> 00:02:59,205
Exactement.
Right.

73
00:02:59,965 --> 00:03:01,565
Je crois qu'il est temps de me tirer...
I think it's time to bail out...

74
00:03:01,645 --> 00:03:03,325
de ce film et de DEMANDER.
of this film and ASK.

75
00:03:47,205 --> 00:03:48,325
Antoine. Des messages ?
Antoine. Any messages?

76
00:03:48,405 --> 00:03:50,405
Oui, plein. Tiens, c'est pour toi.
Yes, tons. Here, this is for you.

77
00:03:51,605 --> 00:03:54,365
-C'est pour toi. -Merci, Benjamin, salut.
-This is for you.
-Thanks, Benjamin, bye.

78
00:03:54,445 --> 00:03:55,805
Benjamin qui ? Biolay ?
Benjamin who? Biolay?

79
00:03:55,885 --> 00:03:57,205
Il réfléchit.
He's thinking it over.

80
00:03:57,285 --> 00:03:58,525
Il aimait beaucoup Mathias.
He really liked Mathias.

81
00:03:58,605 --> 00:04:00,805
Accélère son deuil en mettant ça sur le dos de Mathias.
Speed-up his grieving process
by blaming Mathias.

82
00:04:00,885 --> 00:04:03,245
On ne l'a pas viré, il a abandonné ses clients !
We didn't fire him,
he abandoned his clients!

83
00:04:03,325 --> 00:04:05,205
Et s'il est trop triste, il n'a qu'à écrire une chanson !
And if he's too sad, he can write a song!

84
00:04:05,285 --> 00:04:06,405
Le contrat Dujardin.
The Dujardin contract.

85
00:04:07,725 --> 00:04:09,885
-On a un autre problème. -Quoi ?
-We have another problem.
-What?

86
00:04:10,525 --> 00:04:14,165
Les acteurs de Mathias veulent des agents confirmés. Ils ne nous prennent pas au sérieux, Hervé et moi.
Mathias's actors want senior agents.
They don't take Hervé and me seriously.

87
00:04:14,245 --> 00:04:17,645
C'est vous qui ne vous prenez pas au sérieux. Montrez plus d'assurance.
You don't take yourselves seriously.
Put out more confidence.

88
00:04:17,725 --> 00:04:19,645
Comme essayer d'entrer en boîte quand on est mineur.
Like trying to get into a club as a minor.

89
00:04:19,725 --> 00:04:22,404
La première fois que je suis entré en boîte, j'avais 26 ans.
The first time I got into a nightclub,
I was 26.

90
00:04:22,485 --> 00:04:23,725
Incroyable. Quel pitre.
Unbelievable. What a clown.

91
00:04:23,805 --> 00:04:26,645
S'il y a un problème, organisez des rendez-vous avec Arlette, Gabriel ou moi.
If there's a snag, set up meetings
with Arlette, Gabriel or me.

92
00:04:26,725 --> 00:04:27,725
J'ai dit non !
I said no!

93
00:04:28,565 --> 00:04:30,685
J'ai une réunion à 11h et une semaine chargée.
I have a meeting at 11 am and a full week.

94
00:04:30,765 --> 00:04:31,645
Tu es sourd ?
Are you deaf?

95
00:04:31,725 --> 00:04:32,565
Ça va être compliqué.
Going to be tough.

96
00:04:32,645 --> 00:04:35,965
Sans blague, j'ai déjà eu quatre cafés avec quatre clients différents.
No kidding, I already had four coffees
with four different clients.

97
00:04:36,765 --> 00:04:38,725
Hé ! Pouet, pouet ! Oh, laisse tomber.
Hey! Honk, honk! Oh, never mind.

98
00:04:38,805 --> 00:04:40,005
Oublie le cinquième.
Forget the fifth.

99
00:04:40,725 --> 00:04:42,325
À quelle heure se termine les embouteillages ?
At what time does rush hour end?

100
00:04:42,405 --> 00:04:44,365
-Ça se dégage vers 11h. -D'accord.
-It eases up around 11 am.
-Okay.

101
00:04:45,485 --> 00:04:47,605
Comment se sont passées tes réunions ?
How did your meetings go?

102
00:04:49,085 --> 00:04:52,085
Eh bien, mes réunions se sont passées...
Well, my meetings went...

103
00:04:52,165 --> 00:04:55,285
comme ça, comme ça, et comme ça.
like this, this, and this.

104
00:04:55,845 --> 00:04:56,925
Génial !
Awesome!

105
00:04:57,645 --> 00:04:58,765
-Le grand chelem ! -Ouais !
-The grand slam!
-Yeah!

106
00:04:58,845 --> 00:04:59,965
J'ai aussi une bonne nouvelle.
I also have good news.

107
00:05:01,005 --> 00:05:03,885
-Sofia a cartonné à son audition avec Luchini. -Super.
-Sofia nailed her audition with Luchini.
-Cool.

108
00:05:04,645 --> 00:05:05,765
Qui s'occupe de Cluzet ?
Who's on Cluzet?

109
00:05:05,845 --> 00:05:07,365
Excusez-moi. Allô ?
Excuse me. Hello?

110
00:05:07,445 --> 00:05:08,765
-Bérénice... -Arlette !
-Bérénice...
-Arlette!

111
00:05:10,005 --> 00:05:11,725
-Oui ? -Tu t'occupes de Cluzet ?
-Yes?
-Are you taking care of Cluzet?

112
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:13,605
Je suis désolée.
I'm sorry.

113
00:05:13,685 --> 00:05:15,285
Cluzet, Cluzet, Cluzet.
Cluzet, Cluzet, Cluzet.

114
00:05:15,365 --> 00:05:16,685
Où est Cluzet ? Le voilà.
Where is Cluzet? There he is.

115
00:05:17,445 --> 00:05:19,685
Cluzet, c'est fini. Voilà.
Cluzet is not anymore. There.

116
00:05:20,485 --> 00:05:21,485
Quelle heure est-il ?
What time is it?

117
00:05:21,565 --> 00:05:23,445
Je dois filer, Balasko m'attend.
I have to run, Balasko's waiting.

118
00:05:23,525 --> 00:05:26,165
Le Splendid, c'est comme les huîtres : ça se prend à la demi-douzaine.
Le Splendid are like oysters:
they come in half-dozens.

119
00:05:26,245 --> 00:05:28,405
T'en as un, tu les as tous !
You get one, you get them all!

120
00:05:28,485 --> 00:05:30,005
Qu'est-ce qui s'est passé avec Cluzet ?
What happened with Cluzet?

121
00:05:30,085 --> 00:05:32,565
Il ne veut plus d'agent. Il cloisonne.
He no longer wants an agent.
He's compartmentalizing.

122
00:05:33,125 --> 00:05:34,965
Il a un psy et un avocat.
He's got a shrink and a lawyer.

123
00:05:35,725 --> 00:05:38,325
D'accord. Et Dany Boon, ça avance ?
Okay. And Dany Boon, how's that going?

124
00:05:38,885 --> 00:05:40,965
Tournage à New York. Il ne parle qu'à sa famille.
Shooting in New York.
He only talks to family.

125
00:05:41,045 --> 00:05:43,165
Oui, mais il faut trouver une solution.
Yes, but we have to find a solution.

126
00:05:43,245 --> 00:05:46,565
On ne peut pas se permettre de le perdre. Autant mettre la clé sous la porte.
We can't afford to lose him.
We might as well close shop.

127
00:05:47,565 --> 00:05:48,685
J'en peux plus.
I can't take it anymore.

128
00:05:50,245 --> 00:05:52,845
Mon fils ne reviendra jamais. Mais toi, t'es encore là.
My son will never come back.
But you're still here.

129
00:05:53,325 --> 00:05:54,365
J'ai pas le temps.
I don't have time.

130
00:05:54,445 --> 00:05:55,685
C'est dans le texte ?
Is that in the text?

131
00:05:56,165 --> 00:05:57,285
Non, c'est moi qui parle.
No, that's me talking.

132
00:05:57,845 --> 00:05:59,765
J'ai pas le temps. Je suis vraiment débordé.
I don't have time. I'm really busy.

133
00:05:59,845 --> 00:06:02,245
Ce que je fais ici, ça s'appelle travailler.
What I'm doing here is called work.

134
00:06:02,325 --> 00:06:04,805
Moi aussi je travaille. Mais pas avec toi.
I'm working too.
But I'm not working with you.

135
00:06:05,805 --> 00:06:08,125
Mon agent me propose des auditions, je réponds.
My agent offers me auditions, I answer.

136
00:06:08,405 --> 00:06:11,365
Je connais déjà la scène. C'est comme si on racontait ma vie ici.
I already know the scene.
It's like my life story being told here.

137
00:06:11,925 --> 00:06:14,645
Je vais balancer des trucs bien, le réalisateur va accrocher.
I'll say some cool stuff,
the director will dig it.

138
00:06:14,725 --> 00:06:16,245
Et toi tu vas galérer, comme d'hab.
And you'll struggle, as usual.

139
00:06:16,325 --> 00:06:18,405
Et voilà, fin de journée. C'est bon ?
And that's it, end of the day. All right?

140
00:06:28,765 --> 00:06:29,685
Hé, Dylan.
Hey, Dylan.

141
00:06:30,885 --> 00:06:33,365
Je suis Gabriel Sarda, agent chez ASK.
I'm Gabriel Sarda, agent with ASK.

142
00:06:34,245 --> 00:06:35,685
Non merci. J'en ai déjà un.
No, thanks. I already have one.

143
00:06:35,765 --> 00:06:36,845
Je m'en doute.
So I imagine.

144
00:06:37,965 --> 00:06:39,685
Je voulais te parler de Franck.
I wanted to talk to you about Franck.

145
00:06:40,165 --> 00:06:42,885
Tu sais, Franck est un acteur expérimenté.
You know, Franck is an experienced actor.

146
00:06:42,965 --> 00:06:44,005
Il est vieux comme le monde.
He's old as fuck.

147
00:06:45,325 --> 00:06:48,125
C'est-à-dire, dans vos termes, peut-être. Mais...
I mean, in your words, perhaps. But...

148
00:06:48,725 --> 00:06:50,125
C'est pas facile pour lui.
It's not easy for him.

149
00:06:50,725 --> 00:06:52,125
Tu es dans...
You're in...

150
00:06:52,645 --> 00:06:56,125
Tu es dans ton élément. C'est taillé pour toi, mais pas pour lui.
You're in your environment.
It's tailor-made for you, but not for him.

151
00:06:56,725 --> 00:06:58,685
Il est vieux comme le monde. On est d'accord.
He's old as fuck. We agree.

152
00:07:02,565 --> 00:07:03,645
Tu connais Télérama ?
Do you know Télérama?

153
00:07:04,165 --> 00:07:06,085
-Oui. -C'est plutôt cool, non ?
-Yes.
-It's pretty dope, right?

154
00:07:06,685 --> 00:07:07,645
Je suppose.
I guess.

155
00:07:07,725 --> 00:07:08,805
-Super. -Pourquoi ?
-Cool.
-Why?

156
00:07:09,845 --> 00:07:10,845
Ils me veulent en couverture.
They want me on the cover.

157
00:07:11,925 --> 00:07:13,605
C'est super. Félicitations.
That's great. Congratulations.

158
00:07:13,685 --> 00:07:14,525
Merci.
Thanks.

159
00:07:15,245 --> 00:07:16,485
-Comme je disais. -Merde.
-As I was saying.
-Shit.

160
00:07:17,125 --> 00:07:17,965
Allô ?
Hello?

161
00:07:18,765 --> 00:07:20,405
Ouais. Quoi de neuf ?
Yeah. What's up?

162
00:07:21,685 --> 00:07:23,405
-Bonjour ! -Bonjour.
-Hello!
-Hello.

163
00:07:27,645 --> 00:07:28,485
Bonjour.
Hello.

164
00:07:32,925 --> 00:07:34,325
Ta-da !
Ta-da!

165
00:07:35,285 --> 00:07:36,485
Je t'ai apporté une plante.
I brought you a plant.

166
00:07:37,445 --> 00:07:39,645
Je sais, c'est pas vraiment ton truc,
I know, it isn't really your thing,

167
00:07:39,725 --> 00:07:41,645
mais ça renouvelle l'air et ça apporte de la sérénité.
but it renews the air and brings serenity.

168
00:07:41,725 --> 00:07:43,605
Et puis c'est moi qui l'arroserai de toute façon.
Plus, I'll be the one watering it anyway.

169
00:07:45,445 --> 00:07:47,645
Franchement, wow.
I mean, wow.

170
00:07:47,725 --> 00:07:51,285
C'est l'endroit idéal pour travailler, Monsieur le Producteur.
This is the perfect place to work,
Mr. Producer.

171
00:07:51,365 --> 00:07:54,605
Calme, sérénité, concentration maximale.
Calm, serenity, maximum concentration.

172
00:07:55,125 --> 00:07:57,045
La seule chose qui peut me distraire, c'est toi.
The only thing
that can distract me is you.

173
00:07:58,125 --> 00:07:59,885
Assis au bureau d'en face.
Sitting at the desk opposite.

174
00:08:02,645 --> 00:08:04,005
On partage le bureau ?
We're sharing the office?

175
00:08:07,485 --> 00:08:08,605
Oh mon Dieu.
Oh, my God.

176
00:08:09,285 --> 00:08:10,645
Oh mon Dieu !
Oh, my God!

177
00:08:11,285 --> 00:08:13,925
Tu n'es plus mon assistant, mais mon responsable du développement.
You're no longer my assistant,
but my development manager.

178
00:08:14,005 --> 00:08:16,325
Et je te veux impliqué sur chaque dossier.
And I want you close on each case.

179
00:08:16,405 --> 00:08:18,285
Bien sûr, Monsieur le Producteur,
Of course, Mr. Producer,

180
00:08:18,365 --> 00:08:20,685
je suis votre responsable du développement.
I'm your development manager.

181
00:08:22,485 --> 00:08:25,965
Je peux déjà imaginer la journée du directeur du développement !
I can already picture the day
of the development manager!

182
00:08:26,845 --> 00:08:30,685
9h. Réunion avec le scénariste prometteur.
9 am. Meeting with
the up-and-coming scriptwriter.

183
00:08:30,765 --> 00:08:33,005
Je mentionne en passant mon producteur préféré.
I mention in passing my favorite producer.

184
00:08:33,925 --> 00:08:36,525
Midi ! Déjeuner avec le dernier lauréat du Goncourt
Noon!
Lunch with the latest Goncourt recipient

185
00:08:36,605 --> 00:08:38,804
pour discuter de l'adaptation cinématographique de son roman.
to go over
the film adaptation of his novel.

186
00:08:39,765 --> 00:08:43,285
15h. Retour sur une V2 décevante : « La V1 avait plus de punch ! »
3 pm. Feedback
on a disappointing V2, "V1 had more zing!"

187
00:08:43,804 --> 00:08:45,804
17h. Prévu de voir Tarantino
5 pm. Plans to see Tarantino

188
00:08:45,885 --> 00:08:48,525
mais je dois reporter, je suis en retard à mon rendez-vous.
but I have to postpone,
I'm running late for my meeting.

189
00:08:48,605 --> 00:08:51,645
Je dois convaincre tout le monde de produire le premier film d'un génie
I have to convince everyone to produce
the first film of some genius

190
00:08:51,725 --> 00:08:53,525
parce que j'y crois à 100 %.
because I believe in her 100%.

191
00:08:53,725 --> 00:08:54,885
Et 19h.
And 7 pm.

192
00:08:55,405 --> 00:08:56,565
Enfin.
Finally.

193
00:08:58,725 --> 00:09:00,565
On fait l'amour dans notre bureau.
We make love in our office.

194
00:09:02,325 --> 00:09:05,005
Quoi ? Rien. Je pensais juste qu'on pourrait
What is it?
Nothing. I just thought we could

195
00:09:05,085 --> 00:09:07,205
rester discrets au bureau jusqu'à ce qu'on...
keep things quiet around the office
until we...

196
00:09:07,285 --> 00:09:08,125
soit installés.
get settled.

197
00:09:08,685 --> 00:09:11,285
Mathias, je ne veux plus qu'on se cache.
Mathias, I don't want us to hide anymore.

198
00:09:11,365 --> 00:09:13,125
Au travail ou ailleurs.
At work or anywhere else.

199
00:09:13,765 --> 00:09:16,005
Je t'assure, il faut vraiment qu'on avance là-dessus.
I swear, we really have
to move forward on this.

200
00:09:16,725 --> 00:09:17,605
D'accord ?
Okay?

201
00:09:18,805 --> 00:09:19,885
Entrez !
Come in!

202
00:09:21,765 --> 00:09:23,165
Igor. Comment allez-vous ?
Igor. How are you?

203
00:09:24,245 --> 00:09:25,965
-Bien installé ? -C'est parfait.
-Settled in?
-It's perfect.

204
00:09:26,045 --> 00:09:27,125
Vous vous souvenez de Noémie ?
Do you remember Noémie?

205
00:09:27,605 --> 00:09:29,765
Mais bien sûr, comment allez-vous ?
Why, of course, how are you?

206
00:09:29,845 --> 00:09:31,645
Je suis ravie, monsieur de Serisy.
I am delighted, Mr. de Serisy.

207
00:09:31,725 --> 00:09:35,005
Je suis très enthousiaste à l'idée de la mission qui m'attend.
I'm so excited
about the task that lies ahead.

208
00:09:35,085 --> 00:09:37,285
Moi aussi. Comme vous voyez, j'ai pensé à vous,
I'm thrilled.
As you can see, I thought of you,

209
00:09:37,365 --> 00:09:39,125
j'ai fait monter des scénarios pour vous.
I had screenplays brought up for you.

210
00:09:39,205 --> 00:09:40,365
C'est parfait.
It's perfect.

211
00:09:40,445 --> 00:09:41,645
Vous pouvez faire des résumés.
You can write summaries.

212
00:09:42,925 --> 00:09:43,765
Des résumés ?
Summaries?

213
00:09:43,845 --> 00:09:46,165
Oui. Courts. Comme des fiches de lecture.
Yes. Short ones. Like book reports.

214
00:09:46,765 --> 00:09:48,645
En général, c'est Justine, mon assistante, qui s'en charge
Usually, Justine, my assistant, does this

215
00:09:48,725 --> 00:09:51,245
mais elle est débordée en ce moment. Ça ne vous dérange pas ?
but she's swamped at the moment.
Do you mind?

216
00:09:51,325 --> 00:09:52,285
-Non, non. -Bien.
-No, no.
-Good.

217
00:09:52,805 --> 00:09:53,805
Et félicitations.
And congratulations.

218
00:09:54,965 --> 00:09:56,525
Bravo pour Beauvois !
Well done for Beauvois!

219
00:09:57,365 --> 00:09:58,205
Belle prise.
Nice catch.

220
00:09:59,045 --> 00:09:59,965
J'ai vu une ouverture.
I saw an opening.

221
00:10:00,045 --> 00:10:01,325
Formidable. Formidable.
Wonderful. Wonderful.

222
00:10:01,405 --> 00:10:05,565
La prochaine fois, prévenez-moi d'abord. D'accord ?
Next time, just give me
a head's-up first. Okay?

223
00:10:07,005 --> 00:10:08,245
Je vous laisse.
I'll leave you to it.

224
00:10:09,085 --> 00:10:10,405
Et consultez vos mails.
And check your email.

225
00:10:10,485 --> 00:10:13,125
Je vous ai envoyé un brief pour une négociation.
I sent you a brief for a negotiation.

226
00:10:13,205 --> 00:10:15,125
Parfait. Avec qui ?
Perfect. With whom?

227
00:10:20,045 --> 00:10:22,045
C'est bon pour Nathalie Baye, demain.
It's good for Nathalie Baye, tomorrow.

228
00:10:22,605 --> 00:10:24,605
Super ! Vous avez organisé la réunion dans un café ?
Great! You set up the meeting in a café?

229
00:10:24,685 --> 00:10:26,125
Elle ne peut pas voir ce désordre.
She can't see this mess.

230
00:10:26,205 --> 00:10:29,005
Pourquoi ne pas demander à Mathias de dire à ses clients de rester chez ASK ?
Why don't we ask Mathias
to tell his clients to stay with ASK?

231
00:10:29,645 --> 00:10:31,085
Inutile de jouer les coups tordus.
No reason to pull dirty tricks.

232
00:10:31,165 --> 00:10:34,205
Certainement pas ! Je n'ai pas confiance en votre père, c'est une mauvaise graine.
Certainly not! I don't trust your father,
he's a bad egg.

233
00:10:34,845 --> 00:10:36,205
On ne peut rien lui demander.
We can't ask him for anything.

234
00:10:36,565 --> 00:10:38,045
À propos de quoi ?
About what?

235
00:10:39,685 --> 00:10:40,685
Qu'est-ce que vous faites là ?
Why are you here?

236
00:10:41,245 --> 00:10:44,085
Vous n'avez pas une réunion concernant Sofia et Luchini ?
Don't you have a meeting
regarding Sofia and Luchini?

237
00:10:46,405 --> 00:10:47,245
C'est exact.
That's right.

238
00:10:48,325 --> 00:10:49,525
Je n'ai même pas droit à un café ?
I don't even get a coffee?

239
00:10:49,605 --> 00:10:50,925
On ne peut pas. C'est l'heure de pointe.
We can't. It's rush hour.

240
00:11:09,685 --> 00:11:10,645
C'est une blague ?
Is this a joke?

241
00:11:11,885 --> 00:11:12,805
Ce n'est pas mon style.
It's not my style.

242
00:11:14,165 --> 00:11:15,045
Allez, Mathias.
Come on, Mathias.

243
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:18,885
Tu renverrais un producteur avec une offre aussi nulle.
You'd send a producer packing
with such a crappy offer.

244
00:11:18,965 --> 00:11:20,605
On parle de Fabrice Luchini.
We're talking about Fabrice Luchini.

245
00:11:21,165 --> 00:11:22,525
Et de Sofia Leprince.
And Sofia Leprince.

246
00:11:22,605 --> 00:11:24,125
Et de Sofia Leprince.
And Sofia Leprince.

247
00:11:24,205 --> 00:11:25,805
Mathias. Clairement :
Mathias. Plainly put:

248
00:11:25,885 --> 00:11:29,405
soit tu ajoutes un zéro ici, là, et partout ailleurs
either you add a zero here, here,
and everywhere else

249
00:11:29,485 --> 00:11:32,845
et tu supprimes l'« absence d'intéressement à l'étranger ».
and then you get rid
of the "absence of profit-sharing abroad".

250
00:11:32,925 --> 00:11:34,845
-Soit... -Soit tu prends comme c'est.
-Or...
-Or you take it as it is.

251
00:11:34,925 --> 00:11:36,805
Et je ne dis pas à Dany Boon
And I don't tell Dany Boon

252
00:11:36,885 --> 00:11:39,525
que je suis parti parce qu'ASK est une agence sans avenir.
that I left because ASK is
an agency with no future.

253
00:11:41,045 --> 00:11:42,285
C'est un coup bas.
That's a dirty move.

254
00:11:43,565 --> 00:11:45,885
-Non. -C'est Mathias.
-No.
-That's Mathias.

255
00:11:46,445 --> 00:11:48,725
Non, c'est le métier. Et ce n'est pas personnel.
No, that's the job.
And it's nothing personal.

256
00:11:50,125 --> 00:11:54,325
Tu réaliseras vite que diriger une agence, c'est aussi accepter de perdre des batailles.
You'll soon realize that running an agency
also means accepting to lose some battles.

257
00:11:55,285 --> 00:11:57,245
Tu ne peux pas garder mes clients sans moi.
You can't keep my clients without me.

258
00:11:57,525 --> 00:11:59,685
Beaucoup ont besoin de mon avis pour se décider.
Too many need my opinion
to make up their minds.

259
00:12:00,245 --> 00:12:02,085
Et, comme Camille l'a très justement dit,
And, as Camille rightly said,

260
00:12:02,165 --> 00:12:04,565
il n'y a aucune raison de jouer des coups en vache.
there's no reason to pull dirty tricks.

261
00:12:15,405 --> 00:12:17,045
Bonjour. Votre ticket, s'il vous plaît ?
Hello. Ticket, please?

262
00:12:17,605 --> 00:12:20,325
Ce matin, j'ai pris les mauvaises valises !
This morning,
I grabbed the wrong suitcases!

263
00:12:20,405 --> 00:12:23,045
Pardon. Madre de Dios !
I'm sorry. Mother of God!

264
00:12:23,125 --> 00:12:26,365
C'est ma première fois à Paris. Je suis complètement perdue.
It's my first time in Paris.
I'm completely lost.

265
00:12:26,445 --> 00:12:27,965
No español. Je ne comprends pas.
No Spanish. I don't understand.

266
00:12:28,045 --> 00:12:31,125
Je vais traduire. Elle a oublié son sac avec ses billets.
I'll translate.
She forgot her bag with her tickets.

267
00:12:31,205 --> 00:12:33,205
Oui... Je ne prends jamais le métro ! Je le déteste !
Yes...I never take the subway!
I detest it!

268
00:12:33,285 --> 00:12:35,445
Je le hais ! J'ai d'habitude un chauffeur,
I hate it! I usually have a driver,

269
00:12:35,525 --> 00:12:38,365
mais c'est impossible d'en trouver un dans cette ville !
but it's impossible
to find one in this city!

270
00:12:38,445 --> 00:12:40,045
C'est un cauchemar !
It's a nightmare!

271
00:12:40,125 --> 00:12:41,605
C'est un cauchemar !
It's a nightmare!

272
00:12:41,685 --> 00:12:43,245
No español. Je ne comprends pas.
No Spanish. I don't understand.

273
00:12:43,325 --> 00:12:45,165
-S'il vous plaît ! -Vous avez bien compris,
-Please!
-You understood that,

274
00:12:45,245 --> 00:12:46,525
elle panique.
she's panicking.

275
00:12:46,605 --> 00:12:47,805
-Faites un effort. -Oui, oui.
-Make an effort.
-Yes, yes.

276
00:12:47,885 --> 00:12:50,045
C'est une touriste, soyez gentil, laissez-la passer.
She's a tourist, be nice, let her through.

277
00:12:50,125 --> 00:12:51,165
Oui, s'il vous plaît.
Yes, please.

278
00:12:51,245 --> 00:12:53,445
-Bon, okay, allez, allez. -Merci beaucoup !
-Fine, okay, go on, go, go.
-Thank you very much!

279
00:12:55,565 --> 00:12:56,965
La France en a besoin.
France needs it.

280
00:13:00,285 --> 00:13:01,565
Mademoiselle !
Miss!

281
00:13:02,165 --> 00:13:04,885
Vous avez de la chance. Normalement, ils ne laissent passer personne.
You are lucky. Normally,
they don't let anyone through.

282
00:13:04,965 --> 00:13:07,485
Ouais, ils sont généralement tellement pénibles. Merci de votre aide.
Yeah, they're usually such a pain.
Thanks for your help.

283
00:13:07,565 --> 00:13:08,965
Bonne journée !
Have a good day!

284
00:13:14,405 --> 00:13:16,005
Isabelle Huppert. Vraiment ?
Isabelle Huppert. Really?

285
00:13:16,645 --> 00:13:21,605
Ouais, je peux la coincer entre deux vols, tu as une heure pour faire l'interview.
Yeah, I can catch her between flights,
you can have one hour to do an interview.

286
00:13:21,685 --> 00:13:23,365
Une heure et demie si tout va bien.
An hour and a half on a good day.

287
00:13:23,645 --> 00:13:25,805
Elle a adoré ton article sur la pièce de Bob Wilson.
She loved your piece
on the Bob Wilson play.

288
00:13:25,885 --> 00:13:27,005
-Ah oui. -Ouais.
-Oh, right.
-Yeah.

289
00:13:27,085 --> 00:13:28,445
Je l'ai appelée un « trésor national ».
I called her a "national treasure."

290
00:13:28,525 --> 00:13:29,885
Voilà.
That's it.

291
00:13:30,965 --> 00:13:32,645
Gabriel, explique-moi ça.
Gabriel, explain this to me.

292
00:13:32,725 --> 00:13:34,205
Ça fait des mois que je te dis
I've been telling you for months

293
00:13:34,285 --> 00:13:35,565
qu'on la veut pour Télérama.
we want her for Télérama.

294
00:13:36,085 --> 00:13:38,765
-Et d'un coup... -C'est juste comme ça que ça s'est passé.
-And all of a sudden...
-It's just how things worked out.

295
00:13:39,285 --> 00:13:40,285
Tu as quoi en tête ?
What are you planning?

296
00:13:40,845 --> 00:13:45,725
Rien. En fait, j'ai entendu dire que votre prochaine une serait sur Dylan Charif ?
Nothing. Actually, I've heard you're doing
your next cover on Dylan Charif?

297
00:13:46,205 --> 00:13:47,125
Tu veux le récupérer ?
You want to get him?

298
00:13:47,205 --> 00:13:49,885
Oh, non, pas Dylan. Franck, plutôt.
Oh, no, not Dylan. Franck, rather.

299
00:13:49,965 --> 00:13:50,805
Dubosc ?
Dubosc?

300
00:13:51,605 --> 00:13:53,165
Il ne travaille pas déjà avec vous ?
Isn't he already working with you?

301
00:13:53,245 --> 00:13:55,245
J'aimerais vraiment que tu lui fasses une couverture.
I'd really like you
to do the cover on him.

302
00:13:55,325 --> 00:13:56,765
De quoi tu parles ?
What are you talking about?

303
00:13:56,845 --> 00:14:00,005
C'est sa première fois dans ce genre. Il est très bon.
It's his first time playing in this genre.
He's very good.

304
00:14:00,085 --> 00:14:02,765
Il traverse une crise de légitimité, ça lui ferait du bien !
He's having a legitimacy crisis,
it'd do him some good!

305
00:14:02,845 --> 00:14:06,645
Attends. On ne fait pas des couvertures pour que les acteurs se sentent « bien » !
Hold on. We don't hand out covers
to make actors feel "good"!

306
00:14:07,685 --> 00:14:09,405
Dubosc ? Dans Télérama ?
Dubosc? In Télérama?

307
00:14:10,405 --> 00:14:12,365
-Il est formidable. -Ouais, c'est ça.
-He's terrific.
-Yeah, right.

308
00:14:12,445 --> 00:14:15,765
Tu auras Dylan plus tard, il va tourner sans arrêt !
You'll get Dylan later,
he's going to be shooting non-stop!

309
00:14:15,845 --> 00:14:17,725
Pour Franck, ce serait une reconnaissance.
For Franck, it would be a validation.

310
00:14:19,845 --> 00:14:22,405
Laisse tomber. De toute façon, c'est pas moi qui décide.
Forget it. Anyway, it's not up to me.

311
00:14:22,885 --> 00:14:24,045
C'est Fabienne Pascaud qui décide.
Fabienne Pascaud decides.

312
00:14:24,965 --> 00:14:26,525
Isabelle va être déçue.
Isabelle will be disappointed.

313
00:14:26,605 --> 00:14:29,885
Oh non. Elle croyait avoir décroché l'audition !
Oh, no. She thought
she'd nailed the audition!

314
00:14:29,965 --> 00:14:31,765
Désolé, elle n'était pas le choix de Valérie.
Sorry, she wasn't Valérie's pick.

315
00:14:31,845 --> 00:14:33,765
Je te dis, elle veut un visage !
I'm telling you, she wants a face!

316
00:14:33,845 --> 00:14:35,645
Quelqu'un qui se démarque.
Someone who stands out.

317
00:14:35,725 --> 00:14:37,565
Qui a de la personnalité. Elle veut...
Who has personality. She wants...

318
00:14:37,645 --> 00:14:39,765
un personnage à la Almodovar,
an Almodovar-type of character,

319
00:14:39,845 --> 00:14:41,285
tu vois ce que je veux dire ? Tu vois ?
see what I mean? Do you?

320
00:14:41,365 --> 00:14:44,525
D'accord, Constance, j'y réfléchis et je te rappelle.
Okay, Constance,
I'll think it over and call you back.

321
00:14:45,405 --> 00:14:47,245
C'est pour le film de Valérie Donzelli ?
Is it about the Valérie Donzelli film?

322
00:14:47,325 --> 00:14:49,765
Elle refuse toutes mes actrices. Elles sont « trop banales ».
She's rejecting all my actresses.
They're "too plain."

323
00:14:50,445 --> 00:14:51,725
Tes filles sont bien.
Your girls are good.

324
00:14:51,805 --> 00:14:53,565
Elles sont bien, mais pas assez de relief.
They're good, but not much relief.

325
00:14:54,885 --> 00:14:55,925
Merci de ton aide.
Thanks for your help.

326
00:14:56,005 --> 00:14:59,285
Samuel disait toujours : « Quand elles ne sont pas dans ton fichier, cherche dans la rue. »
Samuel always said: "When they're not
in your file, look in the street."

327
00:15:00,245 --> 00:15:01,285
Regarde Jean Gabin !
Look at Jean Gabin!

328
00:15:02,325 --> 00:15:04,725
Non, pas ici ! Il dort dans mon bureau.
No, not here! He's asleep in my office.

329
00:15:04,805 --> 00:15:05,805
Cherche comme lui.
Search like him.

330
00:15:05,885 --> 00:15:07,565
Il faut les flairer !
You have to sniff them out!

331
00:15:08,125 --> 00:15:10,165
Les débusquer ! Tu vois ?
Track them down! You see?

332
00:15:10,965 --> 00:15:11,885
Attends.
Wait.

333
00:15:12,885 --> 00:15:13,765
Quoi ?
What?

334
00:15:14,725 --> 00:15:15,965
-J'ai trouvé. -Quoi ?
-I've got it.
-What?

335
00:15:16,965 --> 00:15:19,325
Enfin, je ne l'ai pas encore. Mais j'ai trouvé !
Well, I haven't got her yet.
But I've got it!

336
00:15:20,685 --> 00:15:23,045
Merci, Arlette ! Merci, Jean Gabin !
Thanks, Arlette! Thanks, Jean Gabin!

337
00:15:23,685 --> 00:15:24,525
Mais...
But...

338
00:15:49,205 --> 00:15:50,085
Hé !
Hey!

339
00:15:53,125 --> 00:15:54,085
Je suis vraiment désolé.
I'm so sorry.

340
00:15:54,965 --> 00:15:56,125
Non, mais c'est vrai.
No, but it's true.

341
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,085
-Bon appétit. -Merci.
-Bon appétit.
-Thank you.

342
00:15:59,365 --> 00:16:02,285
C'est Vincent, fais attention, quand il parle, c'est comme un tunnel.
That's Vincent, watch out,
when he talks, it's like a tunnel.

343
00:16:02,365 --> 00:16:05,365
Attends. Pas juste un tunnel, un tunnel de mauvaise haleine.
Hold on. Not just a tunnel
but a tunnel of bad breath.

344
00:16:05,445 --> 00:16:06,845
Donc sois prudente.
So be careful.

345
00:16:07,405 --> 00:16:08,525
Merci pour la mise en garde.
Thanks for the heads-up.

346
00:16:08,605 --> 00:16:10,805
Nous les assistants, il faut se serrer les coudes.
We assistants have to stick together.

347
00:16:12,405 --> 00:16:14,485
Je ne suis plus l'assistante de Mathias.
I'm no longer Mathias's assistant.

348
00:16:14,565 --> 00:16:16,045
-Non ? -Non.
-You're not?
-No.

349
00:16:16,125 --> 00:16:18,645
Je l'étais, pendant six ans, chez ASK.
I was, during six years, at ASK.

350
