they alternate. One day, François shoots,
the next day, it's Gilles.

996
00:46:53,325 --> 00:46:57,045
Ça leur permet de travailler plus longtemps et du coup ils ont des tonnes de projets.
It allows them to work longer
and so they have tons of projects.

997
00:46:57,125 --> 00:46:58,245
Je savais pas ça.
I didn't know that.

998
00:46:58,325 --> 00:46:59,445
-Ouais. -Attends,
-Yeah.
-Hold on,

999
00:46:59,525 --> 00:47:01,565
c'est lequel que j'ai rencontré alors ?
which one did I meet then?

1000
00:47:01,645 --> 00:47:03,405
Tu l'as rencontré quel jour ?
On what day did you meet him?

1001
00:47:04,525 --> 00:47:06,845
Attends, c'était... mardi.
Hold on, it was... Tuesday.

1002
00:47:06,925 --> 00:47:07,805
Mardi ?
Tuesday?

1003
00:47:07,885 --> 00:47:10,085
Non, t'as dû voir Gilles.
No, you must have seen Gilles.

1004
00:47:10,165 --> 00:47:12,405
C'est généralement Gilles qui rencontre les acteurs.
It's generally Gilles
who meets with actors.

1005
00:47:12,485 --> 00:47:13,965
Parce que François...
Because François is...

1006
00:47:14,045 --> 00:47:16,765
C'est gênant, mais François postillonne quand il parle.
It's embarrassing,
but François spits when he speaks.

1007
00:47:18,165 --> 00:47:20,325
-Tu me fais marcher ? -Ouais.
-You're bullshitting me?
-Yeah.

1008
00:47:23,205 --> 00:47:25,085
Quel idiot. J'arrive pas à le croire.
What an idiot. I can't believe it.

1009
00:47:25,165 --> 00:47:26,685
-Quel clown. -C'est toi.
-What a clown.
-You are.

1010
00:47:26,765 --> 00:47:28,285
Tu crois tout ce qu'on te dit.
You believe everything you hear.

1011
00:47:31,765 --> 00:47:33,445
Mais c'est pour ça que t'es une bonne actrice.
But that's why you're a good actress.

1012
00:47:34,005 --> 00:47:36,685
C'est touchant, voilà ce que c'est.
It's moving, is what it is.

1013
00:47:41,245 --> 00:47:42,085
Excusez-moi.
Excuse me.

1014
00:47:44,365 --> 00:47:46,845
APPEL ENTRANT
INCOMING CALL

1015
00:47:46,925 --> 00:47:48,445
Viens danser !
Girl! Come dance!

1016
00:47:48,525 --> 00:47:49,605
On y va !
Let's go!

1017
00:47:56,685 --> 00:47:59,605
Et maintenant... mon sucre d'amour !
And now... sugar pie!

1018
00:48:02,965 --> 00:48:04,045
T'es rassasié ?
Are you full?

1019
00:48:04,765 --> 00:48:06,445
Moi, rassasié ? Non, jamais.
Me, full? No, never.

1020
00:48:08,365 --> 00:48:09,205
Je...
I...

1021
00:48:09,765 --> 00:48:11,045
Au revoir !
Goodbye!

1022
00:48:11,125 --> 00:48:12,925
Au revoir, et encore merci !
Goodbye, and thanks again!

1023
00:48:14,405 --> 00:48:15,485
À bientôt !
See you soon!

1024
00:48:19,205 --> 00:48:21,045
-Allô ? -Oui, c'est fait.
-Hello?
-Yes, it's done.

1025
00:48:21,125 --> 00:48:22,925
Dany Boon va signer avec vous.
Dany Boon will sign with you.

1026
00:48:24,565 --> 00:48:27,405
Vous n'avez pas l'air ravi. C'est pas ce que vous vouliez ?
You don't seem thrilled about it.
Isn't this what you wanted?

1027
00:48:27,485 --> 00:48:29,285
Vous n'avez jamais honte ?
Do you ever feel any shame?

1028
00:48:29,845 --> 00:48:30,845
Honte de quoi ?
Shame about what?

1029
00:48:31,325 --> 00:48:33,565
De manipuler les gens ?
About manipulating people?

1030
00:48:34,325 --> 00:48:36,805
C'est une façon de me dire que je n'aurai pas Auteuil ?
Is this a way of telling me
I won't be getting Auteuil?

1031
00:48:36,885 --> 00:48:40,205
Non, c'est une vraie question.
No, it's an actual question.

1032
00:48:41,405 --> 00:48:43,045
C'est notre métier, Élise, on l'a choisi.
It's our job, Elise, we chose it.

1033
00:48:44,525 --> 00:48:46,245
Vous m'envoyez les contrats demain ?
You'll send me the contracts tomorrow?

1034
00:48:46,645 --> 00:48:47,485
D'accord.
Okay.

1035
00:49:01,405 --> 00:49:02,485
Tu m'en sers un aussi ?
Pour me one too?

1036
00:49:10,365 --> 00:49:12,845
J'étais sûr de te trouver ici à cette heure-ci.
I was sure I'd find you here at this hour.

1037
00:49:12,925 --> 00:49:14,925
Ouais, bon. Tu verras.
Yes, well. You'll see.

1038
00:49:16,085 --> 00:49:18,685
Une fois qu'on devient directrice générale, les heures sup' ne s'arrangent pas.
Once you become chief executive,
overtime doesn't improve.

1039
00:49:19,285 --> 00:49:20,565
Je ne verrai rien du tout.
I won't be seeing anything.

1040
00:49:20,645 --> 00:49:23,605
Ils ne m'ont pas choisie pour diriger StarMédia.
They didn't pick me
to be the head of StarMédia.

1041
00:49:25,005 --> 00:49:28,365
Bréhier, ce crétin, a nommé Olivier Dimars à ma place.
Bréhier, that jackass,
named Olivier Dimars instead of me.

1042
00:49:29,325 --> 00:49:30,165
Merci.
Thanks.

1043
00:49:31,205 --> 00:49:34,085
Moins expérimenté, et surtout, bien moins compétent.
Less experienced,
and most of all, much less capable.

1044
00:49:36,445 --> 00:49:37,645
Mais c'est un homme.
But he's a guy.

1045
00:49:39,765 --> 00:49:43,045
Je croyais qu'il suffisait d'être la meilleure et de tenir les autres un peu à distance.
I thought I just had to be the best
and keep the others down a bit.

1046
00:49:46,965 --> 00:49:48,525
Je suis encore naïve, apparemment.
I guess I can still be naïve.

1047
00:49:50,605 --> 00:49:51,805
Je suis désolée.
I'm sorry.

1048
00:50:02,245 --> 00:50:04,485
J'imagine que tu n'es pas venue pour me dire ça.
I don't imagine
you came here to tell me that.

1049
00:50:07,005 --> 00:50:08,765
Dany Boon quitte ASK.
Dany Boon is leaving ASK.

1050
00:50:09,565 --> 00:50:11,365
-Pardon ? -Je voulais te prévenir.
-Excuse me?
-I wanted to warn you.

1051
00:50:12,125 --> 00:50:13,605
Il me rejoint chez StarMédia.
He's joining me at StarMédia.

1052
00:50:15,845 --> 00:50:17,525
-Tu bluffes. -Non.
-You're bluffing.
-No.

1053
00:50:17,605 --> 00:50:18,925
Mathias a fait le nécessaire.
Mathias did the necessary.

1054
00:50:20,445 --> 00:50:21,485
Je suis désolée, Andréa.
I'm sorry, Andréa.

1055
00:50:21,565 --> 00:50:22,965
Toi aussi, tu t'es fait avoir.
You've been had too.

1056
00:50:25,405 --> 00:50:28,965
C'est quoi l'idée ? Voir ma tête quand j'apprendrais la nouvelle, c'est ça ?
So, what's the deal? To see my face
when I'd learn the news, is that it?

1057
00:50:29,885 --> 00:50:31,485
Je voulais te faire une proposition.
I wanted to make you an offer.

1058
00:50:34,525 --> 00:50:35,845
Oh, t'es encore debout ?
Oh, you're still up?

1059
00:50:35,925 --> 00:50:37,685
-Je t'attendais. -C'est gentil.
-I was waiting for you.
-That's nice.

1060
00:50:39,245 --> 00:50:41,085
Il s'est passé un truc de dingue au boulot--
Something crazy happened at work--

1061
00:50:41,165 --> 00:50:42,045
J'ai revu Eva.
I saw Eva again.

1062
00:50:44,965 --> 00:50:46,205
Eva, ton ex ?
Eva, your ex?

1063
00:50:47,285 --> 00:50:48,605
On a couché ensemble.
We slept together.

1064
00:50:51,205 --> 00:50:53,405
-Tu plaisantes ? -Non, pas du tout.
-Are you joking?
-No, not at all.

1065
00:50:55,845 --> 00:50:58,605
-Quand ? -Qu'est-ce que ça change, quand ?
-When?
-Who cares, when?

1066
00:50:58,685 --> 00:51:00,125
Ben moi, ça me change quelque chose. Si.
Well, I care. I do.

1067
00:51:00,205 --> 00:51:02,445
Désolé, mais ça me change quelque chose. Je voudrais savoir.
Sorry, but I care. I'd like to know.

1068
00:51:03,085 --> 00:51:05,605
C'était quand ? Quand j'étais à Bergues,
When was this? When I was in Bergues,

1069
00:51:05,685 --> 00:51:06,725
à vomir mes tripes ?
throwing my guts up?

1070
00:51:07,325 --> 00:51:09,445
Ou quand j'étais aux urgences quand elle s'est cassé la jambe ?
Or when I was in the ER
when she broke her leg?

1071
00:51:09,525 --> 00:51:10,725
Je voudrais savoir
I would like to know

1072
00:51:10,805 --> 00:51:12,685
quand t'as trouvé le temps de sauter cette conne.
when you found the time to nail that cow.

1073
00:51:12,765 --> 00:51:13,925
T'es vraiment condescendant.
You're so condescending.

1074
00:51:14,565 --> 00:51:17,725
Condescendant ? T'es folle ? C'est toi qui devrais t'excuser, là.
Condescending? Are you crazy?
You should be apologizing right now.

1075
00:51:17,805 --> 00:51:19,965
M'excuser ? M'excuser de quoi ?
Apologizing? Apologizing for what?

1076
00:51:20,045 --> 00:51:21,805
De m'occuper de ma fille toute seule ?
For looking after my daughter alone?

1077
00:51:21,885 --> 00:51:23,725
Ou de regarder la télé pendant que toi tu t'amuses ?
Or for watching TV while you have fun?

1078
00:51:23,805 --> 00:51:25,925
Je ne m'amuse pas, merde, c'est mon travail.
I don't have fun, damn it, it's my job.

1079
00:51:26,005 --> 00:51:27,605
Tu comprendras jamais ?
When will you understand?

1080
00:51:28,285 --> 00:51:30,605
C'est pas comme si je t'avais pas demandé de venir.
It's not like I haven't asked you to come.

1081
00:51:30,685 --> 00:51:32,685
Tu ne veux pas laisser le bébé. Tu ne peux pas.
You don't want to leave the baby.
You can't.

1082
00:51:32,765 --> 00:51:34,485
Ouais, il faut que l'un de nous soit là.
Yeah, one of us has to be there.

1083
00:51:36,565 --> 00:51:39,285
C'est ce que j'essaie de faire. Trouver du temps pour la famille.
That's what I'm trying to do.
Make time for the family.

1084
00:51:39,365 --> 00:51:41,965
Laquelle ? La nôtre, ou la grande industrie du cinéma ?
Which family? Ours,
or the great film industry?

1085
00:51:43,925 --> 00:51:46,125
Putain, merde ! Super ! Incroyable !
Fuck, damn it! Great! Amazing!

1086
00:51:46,205 --> 00:51:48,445
-Laissez-moi passer. -Je peux le faire aussi.
-Let me through.
-I can do it too.

1087
00:51:55,005 --> 00:51:57,445
Et tu savais que Jane Birkin n'est pas anglaise ?
And did you know
Jane Birkin isn't English.

1088
00:51:57,525 --> 00:51:59,245
Elle est de Savoie.
She's from Savoy.

1089
00:51:59,325 --> 00:52:00,845
Et son accent, c'est du chiqué.
And her accent is just pretend.

1090
00:52:00,925 --> 00:52:04,205
Non, n'essaie même pas. T'es trop faux pour inventer des trucs.
No, don't even try it.
You're too fake to make stuff up.

1091
00:52:04,285 --> 00:52:05,565
-Je suis faux ? -Oui.
-I'm fake?
-Yes.

1092
00:52:06,165 --> 00:52:07,805
Ouais, bon, mais maintenant...
Yeah, all right, but now...

1093
00:52:08,965 --> 00:52:11,285
Je fais une caipirinha de compète. T'en veux une ?
I make a mean caipirinha. You want one?

1094
00:52:11,765 --> 00:52:12,605
Allez, on y va.
Let's go.

1095
00:52:20,725 --> 00:52:22,725
Au revoir, Camille. Merci, c'était super sympa.
Bye, Camille. Thanks, it was so much fun.

1096
00:52:22,805 --> 00:52:24,365
Te voilà, tout va bien ?
There you are, everything Okay?

1097
00:52:24,445 --> 00:52:25,925
Il y a une grande fête à Saint-Ouen.
There's a big party in St Ouen.

1098
00:52:26,005 --> 00:52:27,405
-On y va ? -C'est quoi l'urgence ?
-Let's go?
-What's the rush?

1099
00:52:27,485 --> 00:52:29,325
Ça va être de la bombe.
It's going to be lit.

1100
00:52:29,405 --> 00:52:30,725
Si t'as besoin d'un transport, on y va.
If you need a ride, let's go.

1101
00:52:30,805 --> 00:52:32,205
-Alright, on y va. -OK.
-All right, let's go.
-Okay.

1102
00:52:33,525 --> 00:52:34,485
Allez, viens !
Come on!

1103
00:52:47,645 --> 00:52:49,605
Camille ? T'as vu Gabriel ?
Camille? Have you seen Gabriel?

1104
00:52:49,685 --> 00:52:52,205
Il vient de partir avec Sarah ! Il n'a pas dit au revoir ?
He just left with Sarah!
Didn't he say goodbye?

1105
00:52:52,285 --> 00:52:53,125
Bien sûr, bien sûr.
Sure, sure.

1106
00:53:53,205 --> 00:53:55,205
Traduction des sous-titres par Céline Nyanga
Subtitle translation by Céline Nyanga
